            <ArticleTitle>Nursing management of a child with juvenile rheumatoid arthritis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>17-22; quiz 23</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Juvenile rheumatoid arthritis is an incurable chronic disease of childhood which involves connective tissue in the joints. Treatment aims are supportive and directed toward pain management, alleviation of inflammation, and optimization of joint function. A multidisciplinary team approach is helpful, with nursing care an essential part of the treatment plan.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
